Z||000000||PAUL88GT||12-20-2001||12:48 PM||||Can someone provide the GM part numbers for the both 86 & 88 V6 ignition modules.  They may be the same part, but it seems I read somewhere they were different.  I plan to order a couple from gmpartsdirect.com to have as spares.  Thanks and Merry Christmas.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000001||GTDude||12-20-2001||08:30 PM||||I don't have the part #'s but they are definitely different.  86 used a distributor module and 88 used a dis module with 3 coils on top.  The 88 ones are VERY expensive.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||12-20-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTDude:<BR><B>I don't have the part #'s but they are definitely different.  86 used a distributor module and 88 used a dis module with 3 coils on top.  The 88 ones are VERY expensive.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>?? What have you been smokin'?  No V-6 Fiero ever came with DIS (just an FYI).  <P>As far as part #'s go, I can't help you there.  I believe that they are the same......there would be no reason why they wouldn't be (same motors, etc.).<P>     <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PAUL88GT||12-20-2001||11:46 PM||||Can someone with a 22P manual help a brutha out?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierobruiser||12-21-2001||12:04 AM||||The 22P lists 2 modules for the V6. The first is  Module ,Distr<BR>(1985 OEM #1103633).....1987466. The second is Module Distr(1985 OEM#1103694)(86-88)....10496269 I'm not sure what is the applicable # but none of them get a hit a GMPARTSDIRECT.COM. <P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
